 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? I usually suggest at least two or three months, so the oil doesn't feel dry on the surface. Then varnish with a thin coat right away, and another coat after you've worn it once. A light oil painting is born. If you use a thin coat of varnish as protective layer, and reapply every few days until the oil is dry, it's not ideal, but it gets the job done. It will feel dry to the touch, and won't leave a film on the paper under a dry fingernail.",
